  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "When team members can be themselves at work, they feel more comfortable sharing and pushing for innovative ideas. The goal is to make your team members feel comfortable doing things differently so that they and the company can continuously improve. \n\n### Why is it important?\n\nWhen a team member feels stressed out or afraid to speak up, he or she may be less honest and experience anxieties that prohibit them from pushing for innovation.\n\nUse these [Tips for a High-Trust Culture](Glint_Team_Tips_for_a_High-Trust_Culture) to get started.",
